OL,3,CWarning issued to public after grass
OL,4,Cfire breaks out near family farm estate
OL,6,F"You can help us to reduce the risk of
OL,7,Fa grass or wildfire, especially during
OL,8,Fspells of hot weather when the ground
OL,9,Fis extremely dry, by not throwing
OL,10,Fcigarettes onto the ground, taking
OL,11,Fyour rubbish home with you, as
OL,12,Freflective litter can easily start a
OL,13,Ffire.
OL,15,F"Not lighting barbecues near grass,
OL,16,Fundergrowth, overhanging branches, or
OL,17,Fproperty, and avoiding having bonfires
OL,18,For campfires when the ground is dry
OL,19,Fand the weather is windy.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/3
